  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hii Mission Technologies obligated $1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies received 81 awards with an average award size of $12.9M. Hii Mission Technologies obligations were down 10.1% year over year. Hii Mission Technologies obligations by fiscal year were $596M in FY21, $657M in FY22, $595M in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, $1.2B in FY25, and $1B in FY26. Hii Mission Technologies top buying agencies in FY2026 to date were the General Services Administration with $847M and the Department of Defense with $196M, followed by the Department of the Interior with $443K, the Department of Education with $388K, the Department of Homeland Security with $18.8K, and the Department of Commerce with $4K. Hii Mission Technologies top markets by NAICS in FY2026 to date were All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $533M and Engineering Services with $469M, followed by Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing with $29.7M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation with $12.2M.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How have obligations trended for Hii Mission Technologies over recent years?",
        "body": "Hii Mission Technologies obligations rose from $596M in FY21 to $657M in FY22, then fell to $595M in FY23 before increasing to $1.1B in FY24 and $1.2B in FY25. Hii Mission Technologies obligations in FY26 are $1B year to date, a change that is down 10.1% year over year."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and markets are driving Hii Mission Technologies' federal business?",
        "body": "Hii Mission Technologies largest buyer in FY2026 to date is the General Services Administration with $847M, followed by the Department of Defense with $196M. Hii Mission Technologies top markets are All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services with $533M and Engineering Services with $469M, with smaller shares in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing ($29.7M) and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation ($12.2M)."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Hii Mission Technologies make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies made $1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies received 81 awards in that period with an average award size of $12.9M. Hii Mission Technologies obligations were down 10.1% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Hii Mission Technologies?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies sells most to the General Services Administration and the Department of Defense. Hii Mission Technologies received $847M from the General Services Administration and $196M from the Department of Defense in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies also received smaller obligations from the Department of the Interior ($443K), the Department of Education ($388K), the Department of Homeland Security ($18.8K), and the Department of Commerce ($4K)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Hii Mission Technologies sell to the government?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies sells professional, engineering, and technical services along with aircraft support and related work. Hii Mission Technologies obligations in All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services were $533M and in Engineering Services were $469M in FY2026 to date. Hii Mission Technologies also had obligations in Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing ($29.7M) and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation ($12.2M)."
